    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Just to get a better sense of how to weigh these risks... if you were comparing two similar developing nations, one that is relatively ethnically homogenous and another that is highly multi-ethnic with various competing groups, would you automatically rank the multi-ethnic one as a higher risk for sudden political shifts or civil unrest? Is there an inherent volatility that comes with that kind of demographic complexity?",
